<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Every user-facing string in the template's own screens, so `VerifyStrings`
  has something to point at and a generated app starts out already following
  the rule rather than inheriting a baseline that suspends it.

  Two things this file is not like Android's `res/values/strings.xml`:
  backslash escapes are NOT unescaped by Compose Multiplatform's converter, so
  write an apostrophe directly and a newline as a real one (the
  `verifyComposeResourceStrings` task in the root build fails on any
  backslash); and the format specifiers are positional `%1$s` / `%1$d`, read by
  `stringResource(Res.string.x, arg)`.

  Keys are prefixed by the screen that owns them. `common_` is for copy that
  really is the same string in more than one place — split it the moment two
  callers want to word it differently.
-->
